 you turn 71 |\n\n**Which is better?** It depends mainly on your current and future tax rates:\n\n- **RRSP** tends to suit people with higher income now who expect a lower tax rate in retirement. The deduction is worth more when your rate is high.\n- **TFSA** tends to suit people with lower income now, those who expect a similar or higher rate later, or anyone who wants flexibility to withdraw without tax. It's also useful for short- to medium-term goals.\n\nMany people use both. The RRSP has a couple of special uses too: the Home Buyers' Plan and the Lifelong Learning Plan let you borrow from your RRSP tax-free, provided you repay it.\n\nContribution limits change yearly, so confirm your personal room on your CRA My Account before contributing. Exceeding your limit triggers penalty tax."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1017,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4607},"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
